cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use EURLC-WGS in your work, please cite it as below, with the
  version you used (eurlc-wgs --version). Please also cite the tools it
  runs; their versions are listed in every report.
title: "EURLC-WGS: whole-genome sequencing analysis of bacterial isolates"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Segerman
    given-names: Bo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8113-8674"
    affiliation: >-
      Swedish Veterinary Agency (SVA), European Union Reference Laboratory
      for Campylobacter, Uppsala, Sweden
version: 1.0.0-rc2
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/BoSegerman/eurlc-wgs"
abstract: >-
  EURLC-WGS takes Illumina reads or assemblies of bacterial isolates and
  runs read QC, species identification and contamination check, assembly,
  MLST, cgMLST (chewBBACA, EFSA-compatible schemas), AMR genes,
  serotyping and virulence genes, and cgMLST clustering, and produces an
  HTML report with a QC verdict per sample. Built first for
  Campylobacter, with specific support for Salmonella, Escherichia coli
  and Listeria monocytogenes.
keywords:
  - whole-genome sequencing
  - bioinformatics pipeline
  - cgMLST
  - Campylobacter
  - Salmonella
  - Escherichia coli
  - Listeria
  - food safety
